WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.400
-This is Jared Leto right here!
-Hey!

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.434
-Welcome back!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:06.467
-Come on, look at this guy.

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:09.734
Let's talk about
"House of Gucci."

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:12.701
Man, you are unbelievable
in this film.

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:16.767
You're amazing, not only the
action and the acting,

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:17.868
but the look.

00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:19.567
They did such a great job.

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:24.334
This is you as Paolo --
Paolo Gucci, look at this.

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:25.667
Yeah, that's Jared.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:26.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:28.701
I know -- were you --

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:30.133
I know you get into
your characters

00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:32.934
when you do your films.
-You could say that.

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:37.200
-Yeah, we once had -- we once
had I'd say probably

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.767
70 percent of the jokes
on our show...

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:40.133
-Maybe.
...and 30 percent

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:42.067
Jared Leto at one time.

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:44.634
But I mean, I love this.

00:00:44.634 --> 00:00:45.734
Do people recognize you?

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:48.501
Do they is go,
"Oh, hey, Jared?"

00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:50.701
-No, I mean, walk around
New York,

00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:54.267
it's pretty great because people
are so nonchalant here.

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:55.267
You know.

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:56.634
"Hey, Jimmy, what's up."

00:00:56.634 --> 00:00:58.334
-Yeah, they don't care,
they've seen everything, yeah.

00:00:58.334 --> 00:01:00.834
-They play it cool.

00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:02.801
But I do have a lot of people
coming up to me

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:04.634
really interested
to see this film

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:08.501
because I didn't know the story
of the Gucci family.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.467
I'm sure a lot of people out
here don't know

00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:11.634
the story of the Gucci family.

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:13.334
-I didn't know.
-And it is shocking.

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:17.801
It's a shocking story
about this dynasty.

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:22.667
It is just Machiavellian and
Shakespearean and all the ends.

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:24.434
It's just an amazingly --
-Yeah.

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:27.300
-It's amazing -- amazingly
complex story,

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.167
and really proud
to be part of it.

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:31.801
Ridley Scott, one of the best
directors in the world.

00:01:31.801 --> 00:01:33.634
-Ridley Scott crushed this.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:36.033
He was -- this was kind
of outside his thing.

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:37.100
I wouldn't even see Ridley
doing this movie.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.000
-You know, he can do anything,
you know,

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.667
from "Alien" to "Gladiator"
to "The Martian,"

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:44.067
and on and on and on.

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:46.300
The guy just made some of my
favorite films of all time.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:48.067
And Al Pacino plays my dad.

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:49.133
-Stop right there.

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:51.400
I mean, I would freak.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:52.667
Have you met him before?

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:54.534
-You know, it's funny
because I showed up

00:01:54.534 --> 00:01:57.868
for the first day of work
in character and I went up

00:01:57.868 --> 00:01:59.667
and I said, "Papa," you know?

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:01.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:04.133
And he looked over and kind of
just skirted away from me.

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:07.467
I said, "Oh, maybe he's a little
grumpy, I don't know."

00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:10.200
-Yeah, of course.
-And then, tried again.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:14.400
I said "Papa, it's me Paolo,"
and he basically

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.300
shuffled off again,
"Like, who is this creep?"

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:22.667
And then someone whispered
to him, "Al, it's Jared."

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:25.901
And he turned around, he said,
"Oh, my son! My son!"

00:02:25.901 --> 00:02:28.501
-My son! [ Smooches ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:28.501 --> 00:02:30.734
-My son!

00:02:30.734 --> 00:02:32.067
-Everyone, it's phenomenal.

00:02:32.067 --> 00:02:34.567
Obviously Lady Gaga
is fantastic,

00:02:34.567 --> 00:02:36.868
but man, I'm not
just saying this,

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:39.033
Jared Leto, watch this dude.

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.801
Watch this guy.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:02:42.801 --> 00:02:45.267
Here's Jared Leto and Lady Gaga
in "House of Gucci."

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:46.467
Take a look at this.

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:48.434
-You have a gift,
I'm telling you.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.300
-Oh, stop.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.501
Stop, you're going to make me --

00:02:52.501 --> 00:02:55.501
you're going to make me cry.

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:57.667
Nobody has ever said that to me.

00:02:57.667 --> 00:02:59.934
Nobody.

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:02.300
-Paolo, why don't you
have your own life?

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:05.501
-Oh, these are just mock ups.

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:08.000
I can't afford to get serious.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.934
-With your gift and your talent
and your vision,

00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:12.267
are you kidding?

00:03:12.267 --> 00:03:14.467
Gucci needs new blood.

00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:16.634
Good-bye 1930s.

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:18.834
Hello '80s, huh?

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:22.834
-[Indistinct] is right up
my guards.

00:03:22.834 --> 00:03:25.234
-Paolo Gucci is coming.

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:28.300
-[ Humming ]

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.834
-That's Jared Leto everybody!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:36.300
Paolo Gucci, "House of Gucci"
is in theaters November 24th.

